Feature: The computer commander
  A computer can command a team. It looks at the map of its team once each second, and it gives
  each drone an order. It sends one drone to each tower that its team does not hold, nearest
  towers first. Each tower goes to the drone that is nearest to it. A drone keeps its order
  until its team holds the tower.

  When drones of the two teams circle a tower, the drone that arrived later is often behind:
  the control is on the side of the other team. A drone that is behind at a contested tower for
  10 s gives up. It goes to a tower that no drone of its team is sent to, and it does not come
  back for 30 s. Thus two commanders do not stop each other at every tower.

  When the commander sees an enemy drone within 120 m of a tower that its team holds, it defends
  the tower first. That is two circles out: an enemy drone that circles the next tower is not a
  danger. It sends the drone that is nearest to the tower. The commander uses only the map of its
  team. Thus it does not know about an enemy drone in the fog.

  Expectation: At the start, the commander sends a drone to each neutral tower
    Each tower goes to the drone that is nearest to it. The centre tower goes to the drone in the
    middle. The flank towers go to the drones at each end.

    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    And the order of the second Blue drone is take the centre tower
    And the order of the third Blue drone is take the east tower

  Expectation: The commander defends a tower that an enemy drone comes near
    Overrides: At the start, the commander sends a drone to each neutral tower
    A tower that the team holds comes first. The other drones go on to the neutral towers.

    Given the Red scout is near the Blue home tower
    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the order of the second Blue drone is take the Blue home tower

  Expectation: A drone that is behind at a contested tower goes somewhere else
    Given the control of the west tower is -20 %
    And the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    And the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 1
    When the computer commander of Blue plays for 15 seconds
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the Red home tower

  Expectation: The commander sends a drone with a low battery home
    Overrides: At the start, the commander sends a drone to each neutral tower
    The commander sends a drone home when its battery is down to 60 s, and the time to fly home,
    and 15 s more. The drone goes back to work when its battery is 90 % full.

    Given the batteries are on
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 80 s
    And the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is go home
